As per the format, '2024-05-04T09:35:47.1Z' is invalid, the parse error is thrown. Please check your server.
@balamurugana, minio (RELEASE.2024-01-16T16-07-38Z) returns the date in this format
@balamurugana Go truncates by removing the trailing 00's. It is not strictly needed; this is similar to retention date parsing AFAICS.

@harshavardhana expiration is [ResponseDate](https://github.com/minio/minio-java/blob/master/api/src/main/java/io/minio/messages/ResponseDate.java) type and we are already taking care of two formats 
```java
  public static final DateTimeFormatter RESPONSE_DATE_FORMAT =
      DateTimeFormatter.ofPattern("yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH':'mm':'ss'.'SSS'Z'", Locale.US).withZone(UTC);
```
```java
  public static final DateTimeFormatter MINIO_RESPONSE_DATE_FORMAT =
      DateTimeFormatter.ofPattern("yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH':'mm':'ss'Z'", Locale.US).withZone(Time.UTC);
```

Previously we faced the same issue from the server and the server got fixed.

