problem_statement:
commands: Provide examples for chromastyles `--highlightStyle` and `--linesStyle`
Running `hugo gen chromastyles` without any flags will generate an `.hl` class that sets the background color. But if you attempt to change the background color with the `--highlightStyle` flag, the `color` gets set instead of the `background-color`:
```
$ hugo gen chromastyles | grep LineHighlight
/* LineHighlight */ .chroma .hl { background-color:#d8d8d8 }

$ hugo gen chromastyles --highlightStyle "#abcdef" | grep LineHighlight
/* LineHighlight */ .chroma .hl { color:#abcdef }

```

```
$ hugo version
hugo v0.125.0-a32400b5f4e704daf7de19f44584baf77a4501ab+extended darwin/amd64 BuildDate=2024-04-16T15:04:41Z VendorInfo=brew
```

hints_text:
```text
$ hugo gen chromastyles --highlightStyle "#fff000 bg:#000fff" | grep LineHighlight
/* LineHighlight */ .chroma .hl { color:#fff000;background-color:#000fff }
```

This isn't documented. Changing issue title.

